IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr1-reg08-09-application`
IMPORT `mlr1-reg18-20-policies`

-- TESTS for regulations 18 to 20.  The duty checklists are tested from their own specification: every condition met answers JUST TRUE;
-- one condition not met answers JUST FALSE; an "unless" exception met answers JUST TRUE; a "where" limit not reached answers JUST TRUE (no requirement has arisen: ruling 2026-11-05, (b), fork F-where); a scope limit not reached answers NOTHING.
-- Inputs are positional, in the order of the function's GIVEN (the conditions, then the "unless" exception, then the "where" limit, then the scope limit).

§ `The duty checklists of regulations 18 to 20`
-- reg 18(1)
#ASSERT `reg 18(1) the relevant person has taken the steps paragraph (1) requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 18(1) the relevant person has taken the steps paragraph (1) requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 18(1) the relevant person has taken the steps paragraph (1) requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
